# Lab 06 – Create and Manage LVM Logical Volumes

## Objective

Initialize an available 400 MB disk for use with LVM, create a Physical Volume (PV), create a Volume Group (`vg200`) with an 8 MB Physical Extent (PE) size, create two Logical Volumes (`lv200` and `lv300`), initialize the logical volumes with different file system types, create mount points, configure persistent mounting through `/etc/fstab`, and verify the final configuration.

---

## Background

LVM (Logical Volume Management) provides an abstraction layer between physical storage and file systems.

The basic LVM hierarchy used in this lab is:

```text
Physical Disk
     ↓
Physical Volume (PV)
     ↓
Volume Group (VG)
     ↓
Physical Extents (PE)
     ↓
Logical Volumes (LV)
     ↓
File Systems
     ↓
Mount Points
```

The lab used a 400 MB disk and configured an 8 MB Physical Extent size.

The requested Logical Volumes were:

* `lv200` → 120 MB
* `lv300` → 100 MB

Because LVM allocates storage in whole Physical Extents, the 100 MB request could not be represented exactly using 8 MB extents.

